Relevant columns and how they might be used
• bigquery-public-data.iowa_liquor_sales.sales  
  - date : filter to 2022 and extract month  
  - county : filter to ‘DUBUQUE’  
  - category_name : filter to ‘BOURBON WHISKEY’  
  - sale_dollars : numerator for “sales” (could also use bottles_sold or volume_sold_liters, but ‑‑ we’ll use dollars)  
  - zip_code : join key to population (cast/trim to 5 digits)  

• bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010  
  - zipcode : join key to liquor‑sales zip  
  - minimum_age / maximum_age : select only records where minimum_age >= 21 (or NULL & minimum_age>=21)  
  - population : denominator for per‑capita figure  
  - gender : we will use rows where gender IS NULL (overall population) so that the numbers aren’t split by sex  

Typical conditions you’ll see
  category_name = 'BOURBON WHISKEY'  
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)=2022  
  county = 'DUBUQUE'  
  SAFE_CAST(SPLIT(zip_code,'.')[OFFSET(0)] AS STRING) = zipcode  
  (gender IS NULL) AND minimum_age >= 21  

